            <ArticleTitle>[A gymnast with painful wrists].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>A5899</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 11-year-old female gymnast presented with long-standing bilateral wrist pain. Radiographs showed physeal widening and irregularity of the left distal radial and ulnar metaphyses, and irregularity of the right distal radial and ulnar metaphyses without physeal widening. 'Gymnast wrist' was diagnosed and cessation of strenuous activities was advised.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
